{
  "slug": "chocolate-sour-cream-cupcakes",
  "title": "Chocolate Sour Cream Cupcakes",
  "blurb": "Soft chocolate cupcakes made with soy flour and enriched with sour cream for a tender crumb.",
  "steps": [
    "Heat your oven to 180°C and line a 12-hole muffin tin with paper cases.",
    "Whisk together the soy flour, cocoa powder, baking powder and salt in a bowl.",
    "In a separate large bowl, beat the sugar and eggs together until pale and slightly thickened, then mix in the sour cream, oil and vanilla extract.",
    "Fold the dry ingredients into the wet mixture until just combined, then stir in the boiling water to create a thin batter.",
    "Divide the batter evenly between the paper cases, filling each about two-thirds full.",
    "Bake for 18 to 20 minutes until a skewer inserted into the centre comes out clean, then cool on a wire rack."
  ],
